# Database Patterns

## Migrations

- One migration per feature or phase, named `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_descriptive_name.sql`
- Every new table must have: RLS enabled, appropriate policies, indexes on foreign keys, `updated_at` trigger
- Always include both "up" logic and a comment describing what would need to be undone

## Queries

- One query file per entity in `src/lib/queries/`
- Every query function must be typed: return `Promise<EntityType[]>` or `Promise<EntityType | null>`
- Use Supabase client query builder, not raw SQL
- Handle errors gracefully: return empty arrays or null, log errors server-side
- Name queries clearly: `getEventById`, `getQuotesByPartner`, `getLeadsByEvent`

## Row-Level Security

- Every table must have RLS enabled — no exceptions
- Customer data scoped to their account via `user_account_id()`
- Internal users see all via `is_internal_user()`
- Partner data scoped to their partner record
- Never bypass RLS in application code unless using the service role for seeding/admin
